      "title": "Gaze \u2014 all providers on MPIIGaze (Original)",
      "note": "FaceMesh detected 2268/3000 faces on MPIIGaze's own evaluation subset (much of it captured in near-dark rooms, so detection confidence is lowered to 0.15; the recovered faces were checked against MPIIGaze's manually annotated eye corners and land within 3.6 px median on a 1280x720 image, so they are real detections rather than noise). Every provider is scored on those same images through the app's real front end. The three classical providers output a screen-space signal rather than an angle, so each gets the per-user calibration the app itself performs (gain + head-pose assist + centre for the geometric/pupil mappers, the full 8-term polynomial for iris_polynomial), fitted per participant on half their samples and scored on the held-out half. The custom CNN is fitted the same way, because the app does the same thing to it (gaze.custom.gain_x/gain_y plus set_center) and because its training labels live in MPIIGaze's normalised frame, not this camera frame. IMPORTANT: this table is a harness for comparing providers against each other on equal terms, and its custom column is NOT comparable to the 93.5% / 2.43\u00b0 in the regressor table above \u2014 that number scores the CNN on MPIIGaze's pre-normalised eye patches (its training domain, and the standard protocol the literature reports), whereas this one crops live from the original image via FaceMesh exactly as the running app does. The gap between the two is a genuine train/serve difference, not a scoring error.",
