  "notes": [
    "mp_geometry (head pose) reports pose relative to a per-user neutral face cloud, so it has no absolute output to score against a dataset; see the runtime tables for its live performance.",
    "The classical blink detectors (EAR standard/adaptive, ELA) are geometric rules over FaceMesh eye landmarks, so scoring them needs full-FACE images labelled open/closed. Every eye dataset on this machine (mrlEyes_2018_01 and both archive copies) contains cropped eye images with no surrounding face, which FaceMesh cannot process, and no full-face set here (300W-LP, AFLW2000, MPIIGaze) carries eye-state labels. They are therefore compared in the runtime tables only; a labelled face set such as CEW (Closed Eyes in the Wild) would be needed to score them against the blink CNN's MRL-Eye numbers. This gap is stated rather than filled with a proxy metric."
